{"title":"G285 2021 MC10A","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that minimizes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9491d8fb9dfa0719338b49d4137e56f266369a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|||2^{|x^2|} - 4|-4|-8|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"23\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7bec1d72bb04ba11e98fe56daab52133be79a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ -1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"393\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denotes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90411c85187d18b9a249b550e144d0c620ba8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{1,2,3 \\cdots n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. Then, a subset of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19fc9a7c409ebdd93a78525007732f60a699fafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;k&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" /> is chosen. All even digits in the subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are then are put into group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and the odd digits are put in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Then, one number is selected at random from either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> with equal chances. What is the probability that the number selected is a perfect square, given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/2/9025128100517777b2b94cfa703bf5dfdad918e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{3}{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{6}{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{7}{13}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"395\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a unit square. If points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively such that the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac3db81a323d4df2e07bbd086547ead8faef5fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEF = \\frac{3}{2} \\triangle CFE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/8328c1f15f556443d67c973e5b582d15247abbb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF^2$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d213c11b909d248dc38e99a9c3d0207cbdaceb64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{13}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{8}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{37}{36}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{13}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"394\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c04529af8584ed9da4c4f2c6565da57c149212.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{18k} \\equiv 76 \\mod 100\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d1409e4d82f9888450288011df631f57e6146f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a recursive sequence be denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea47b324908b7a67b59b71b4cb31334dfb4fe943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/26715e2bf4edeb0e76ffafa3483d22c26ca6a05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fd5b2607a5f82b63fbdc767b69ae09d299d198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1} = n+a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. Let an infinite arithmetic sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b907c23e2dc1bbbf73cabe7cfa7c29831439ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=\\{k+1, k-p+1, k-2p+1 \\cdots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"295\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is prime, for what value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> will <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/826ec989205f1fae6f2f92fa4f4e2d817e45380b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{2021} = k-2022p+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a8e1b18ae0fa92d0d61fe46f6b84803f2666d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1011\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1011}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2021\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{2021}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4042$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"492\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be42c9022f43f7734fa4bf1fc24295a4aa2fe38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k=wv_1+xv_2\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a215504c9223523b8b31283cc8517229189007d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[l=yv_1^2+zv_2^2\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a90edc23e80afeba2bf921e7a7ec6094b6589b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=2w , z=2x\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c09383f52ff7db11358e4aa6ca6c0307b02d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f5be16d8e6ba9772c9fe4d4352ebc00d48b080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,z,k,l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular tetrahedron has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose on the center of each surface, a hemisphere of diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is constructed such that the hemisphere falls inside the volume of the figure. If the ratio between the radius of the largest sphere that can be inscribed inside the old tetrahedron and new tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4e7b264d7d60ad4b71191c2f5c31a800cf9547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m\\sqrt{n}}{r\\sqrt{n}-e}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"67\" height=\"43\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is square free, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c2770e354d7432511dcfd0dde09ca1f1e2d883c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(m,e,r) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c49be78e596eea57c1282ad3b588e0f04231c93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+r+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72292e7183f4cff5d2f60a2cffb30d681a1daf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 19\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 21\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 22\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 23\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/30801ae5adefda97ea3f458d58a2c5e61b241ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\cos 20^o + \\sin 20^o)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad162a753560f243e0a2b39f58d4426f3f63f614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{t}+u}{vx}+w(y^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"43\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is square free and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d020e8866078d00b638e2d860eb315fa53dd7a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(u,v,w) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d4c888ea70d2b7d4c3dcf4fbb4c9c0c12fafb3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+u+v+w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268c004d285a385f098b351e50458a2dabefcad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\cos 20^o$\" width=\"86\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/6/d568de66c49ed55434c24ce6a465bd38b3149919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin 20^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf6611ce10e07eb04026b80310df3fc2659dad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207f2dbaba1482c6121d34b412b51735736b0e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$happy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6235462e115e8c257a805c1dbc698b2740dd11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^3+5k-3 \\ge (k-1)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"19\" />. If a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />  is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb71d3a9590fc31d91feea31109c73e3edf2307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$unhappy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154399879a0312695a49305358a6a2f1ea3059cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^3+5l^2 \\ge 2064l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" />. If a number is neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207f2dbaba1482c6121d34b412b51735736b0e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$happy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb71d3a9590fc31d91feea31109c73e3edf2307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$unhappy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, it will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51770fcd19aae2d35818e3213e2ae739f800681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$neutral$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />. What is the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> randomly selected numbers from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55474291e7988b1edc5e888205512c21241a430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1,100]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> are  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207f2dbaba1482c6121d34b412b51735736b0e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$happy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb71d3a9590fc31d91feea31109c73e3edf2307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$unhappy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51770fcd19aae2d35818e3213e2ae739f800681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$neutral$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />, in any given order?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c144d586e3b70aaf071ce308775b09c850b70c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{20,007}{5,000,000}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{6,669}{1,000,000}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{247}{35,937}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{494}{11,979}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"598\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the sum of its side lengths. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the circumcircle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243b664a2cc9b2c07c54b60df6dca244911f035d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f506b80246907627b4826e4d0fddd0a15f5913c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b34d542adc19c5b24f8dd4bc51eee62ccd9080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"360\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edae70ddedf89e790936ed4035c5ca1480212e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denote the number of integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that each is relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the number of 3-digit positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f5b076691aea10868810aa5a597d4d0ffbeec45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(a)+\\phi(b) \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cc1664dcfded73746515026e0ce71a40e4c854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(b)+\\phi(c) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a recursive sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b02a491e6fc8db3a577b344b1a53b7a8e77e0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad2df3ba15da6fa2569018249132168f45ba256.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> be defined as: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e858431bfa715ea7063c8bb69a439dc27a880c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n = \\frac{2a_{n-1}+3a_{n-2}}{6n}\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"37\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a monic polynomial with real roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1461293dfadef03b6187e43eb256e0e9dc0c71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{r_1,r_2,r_3,r_4 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />. If each root is the reciprocal of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e3aaa8cb9290bdcf54e73e87a5ed17d46c335e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(a_n)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, find the reciprocal of the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a540cfc318445da3572d3de14f4e50fd7bcdb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lceil Q(-1) \\right \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let an ellipsoid centered at the origin have radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff5a0b2f40f1c5660e2825d6afd91fdc14c8622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x,y,z \\} = \\{3,18,24 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />. If a cross-section of the figure is taken at an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af047d634edff061abf160cf57e73eb9672f379e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> to the horizontal base that lies along the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axes, find the area of the cross-section.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b774ccfe1c94cea3e409e3341a9df7427624bed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=1}^{50} s^3 \\sum_{h=3}^{10} {4h+5}\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62ac51192b360323c777edf254f50c71fdc74c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 323400\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 336600\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 673200\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 646800\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2124150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"584\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is a recursive sequence with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0cc1baf84844a02069bd007c932c1486f84649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa221d2d61feb1b7f295e801e6e2bbe9d31761f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}=n \\cdot a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"12\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e25b67b0b0ecf3d282399ca82a0ea85cc94786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_{5}}{a_{k}}=\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63eb1ee41a9e7c646bcb03b7a4651acb730dee8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2&lt;k&lt;7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cded50e10ea3761eb95c3cc69c43d786ced1a9d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum a_2\\]\" width=\"44\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/8709fac817a99f445549d61052ee710ded608dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2,2- 2\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" /> on the Cartesian Plane, where points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie in its interior. Let the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7e55204a315e0916e03fd61b5e8b9550cbcaab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEP$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e5a266b8a03dd97e5f43003941f4fde50077f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDP$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9c561e35a68a37bfc25fb574154f2b9fbd5e54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2+ \\sqrt{3}:6- \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />, the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/63519827794d69a2ae9aaf52d244205cb79c0235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXB$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c0c74e96cf7932b2b71c339553da567930f310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EXD$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d7ee4016c6af9f14d7b8b9d9652e36e9137994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dcef2827737e5839598dff95eb598b0fd92aadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY \\parallel AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d4fabcee7700b51e2ce77e9635380c678e5d60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX=PY$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />. Now, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e07c249c191e13fa5f6b1c38620fa5ff30e42cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PXY$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> can be rotated about point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> degrees counterclockwise to form a new triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a9345870e6b5d4d7c071350b1bbfc83d3aa3c61e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;X&#39;Y&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, such that if the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a989d6f7a22bc7a95ad838e2b562d11ef16bd5df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39; = (x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64bbf5472787021293527e135fb1beac6b4f1b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X&#39; = (x_2,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b8708c17d23e29a6664f425df4f82c2ffc99053e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y&#39; = (x_3,y_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f516ca4a4f5de77d586be4f8d1cc657bd18dff81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=0}^{3} x_i = - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{147}}{5} \\sum_{j=0}^{3} y_j\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"52\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6addc13fc87f69d18b41db754eb12baab6a21ef8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_3-x_2=x_2-x_1= -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} y_3-y_2 = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} y_1-y_2\\]\" width=\"381\" height=\"41\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3918857051a75a035d5547e7d44b5ac63add5035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+x_1+x_2+x_3+y_1+y_2+y_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"250\" height=\"14\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85eb1b1a8fd227abc3936ec427215734ab076e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d-\\frac{n \\sqrt{a}}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"69\" height=\"42\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f9e12c0dd07893f41d855aab7657aa49851b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+n+a+p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/64817d7d7381771719f1152a5817ba0f04b878e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 64\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 67\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 74\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 81\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 23 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a42c9ef976e064fdad9938e3d60d69b0920eed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_p (a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> denote the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />'s in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b267b0afc95c0a669bde43a08b3a7d8908b3939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n} &lt; k &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, find the largest sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c9bea668f84e83795d27b6eb8d4c49e8f4c093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d00faf19b3253a2f615e81c661df4f24fe807c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=k}^{n} \\binom{n-i}{i} v_p(i) &gt; (1+k)^n\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10A Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085216\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 791/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 26788/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21270:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018085216 and revision id 156666. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}